    "Dokdo: The Beautiful Island of Korea": "独島：美しい韓国の島",
    "First integrated into Korean territory in 512 AD by Silla Dynasty General Isabu, Dokdo has stood as an integral part of the Korean nation for over 1,500 years. This majestic volcanic island in the East Sea (Natural Monument No. 336) is renowned for its incredible marine biodiversity, towering basalt structures, and its timeless significance as a symbol of Korean sovereignty and natural majesty.": "西暦512年、新羅の異斯夫（イサブ）将軍が于山国を服属させて以来、1500年以上にわたり韓国固有の領土です。天然記念物第336号に指定され、豊かな海洋生態系と荘厳な柱状節理を誇る、韓国の主権と美しい国土の永遠の象徴です。",
