    "The mystical jade-green inlay glaze craft & floating crane graphics": "神秘的高丽翡翠色瓷釉、独创的嵌瓷技艺与飞鹤纹样",
    "The austere beauty of raw wood grains & Joseon Scholar's lifestyle": "原木天然纹理的质朴美，反映了朝鲜儒生的高雅风操",
    "The ultimate pinnacle of Baekje art, metal gilding, and Taoist cosmology": "百济金属铸造工艺之最高杰作，描绘了道家神仙世界",
    "A monumental, spherical white porcelain jar crafted during the mid-to-late Joseon Dynasty. Rather than showing flawless geometry, the Moon Jar is formed by joining two separate wheel-thrown halves, resulting in a gentle, organic, and beautifully asymmetrical shape resembling a full moon.": "朝鲜中后期制作的代表性白磁大罐。它并非追求完美的几何对称，而是将两个半球合二为一烧制而成，形成了一种浑然天成、宛如温润满月的自然非对称曲线美。",
    "Discovered in the massive tumuli tombs of Gyeongju, these breathtaking crowns are made of pure sheet gold, adorned with complex jade comma-shaped beads (gogok) and tiny golden spangles. They symbolize the sacred cosmic tree connecting heaven and earth.": "出土于庆州新罗大古墓，由纯金薄板打造。冠上缀满绿色的逗号形曲玉和亮闪闪的金片，象征着联结天地的宇宙生命树与飞鸟信仰，极尽华丽。",
    "A crowning architectural masterpiece of the Golden Age of Buddhist art in the Silla Kingdom. It features stone terraces, staircases of exquisite stone masonry, and twin pagodas, Seokgatap and Dabotap, which stand as towering emblems of classical symmetry and Buddhist cosmological ideals.": "新罗黄金时代佛教艺术的巅峰之作。精致的叠石台基、石雕艺术石阶以及东侧多宝塔和西侧释迦塔，展现了古典均衡美与佛教净土理想。",
    "The original document describing 'Hangeul'—the native phonetic script of Korea, commissioned by King Sejong the Great in 1443. Designed to be easily learned by the common people, its elegant alphabetic letters mimic the vocal organs during speech, representing one of the most scientific scripts in human history.": "世宗大王于1443年主持创制的朝鲜本土拼音文字的理论阐述文献。旨在让平民百姓易学易用，其字母构形模仿发音器官，是人类历史上最科学、最具民主精神的文字之一。",
    "A breathtaking volcanic island cluster situated in the East Sea of South Korea, designated as Natural Monument No. 336. Formed millions of years ago by deep-ocean volcanic eruptions, it features dramatic vertical basalt cliffs and pristine, rich marine ecosystems. Recorded historically as Korean territory since the Silla Dynasty (512 AD) when General Isabu integrated the island kingdom of Usan-guk, Dokdo remains a beloved, eternal symbol of Korea's beautiful geography and sovereign pride.": "大韩民国最东端的火山群岛，被指定为第336号天然纪念物。由于深海火山喷发形成，拥有壮丽的柱状节理和原生态海洋生态，自新罗时代起，历来为韩国领土，是国土尊严与主权的象征。",
    "Gastronomy (Hansik)": "韩食料理（Hansik）",
    "Traditional Arts & Crafts": "传统工艺与艺术",
